# XCU lex
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# lex followed by c17 on the generated lex.yy.c; the test programs define
# their own yywrap and main so the lex library is not needed. Missing c17
# makes the test UNRESOLVED. Statistics output is implementation-defined and
# never examined.

assertion  XCU.lex.001
anchor     utilities/lex.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/lex.html#OUTPUT FILES
class      conditional
when       CD
since      1992
says       lex -t writes the C program to standard output and leaves no
           lex.yy.c; without -t the program is written to lex.yy.c; with no
           file operand the source is read from standard input; the program
           compiles.
test       t/001-stdout-and-file.sh

assertion  XCU.lex.002
anchor     utilities/lex.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       CD
since      1992
says       The longest match wins, a tie goes to the earlier rule, unmatched
           input is copied, yytext and yyleng describe the match and
           trailing context r/x matches only r.
test       t/002-matching-rules.sh

assertion  XCU.lex.003
anchor     utilities/lex.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       CD
since      1992
says       A name defined in the definitions section is substituted for
           {name}; %s start conditions keep unprefixed rules active, %x
           conditions disable them, BEGIN switches and INITIAL (or 0)
           returns.
test       t/003-definitions-states.sh

assertion  XCU.lex.004
anchor     utilities/lex.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       CD
since      1992
says       REJECT executes the next best rule for the same input, an action
           of | shares the next rule action, and unput returns a character
           to the input.
test       t/004-reject-pipe-unput.sh

assertion  XCU.lex.005
anchor     utilities/lex.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       CD
since      1992
says       yymore appends the next match to yytext and adjusts yyleng,
           yyless keeps the first n characters and rescans the rest, and
           input reads and consumes the next character.
test       t/005-yymore-yyless-input.sh

assertion  XCU.lex.006
anchor     utilities/lex.html#OPERANDS
anchor     utilities/lex.html#STDIN
class      conditional
when       CD
since      1992
says       Several file operands form one lex program, a - operand is
           standard input, and -t works with them.
test       t/006-operands.sh

assertion  XCU.lex.007
anchor     utilities/lex.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       CD
since      1992
says       Double-quoted text is literal, octal and hex escapes give
           characters, an interval applies to a substituted name, ^ and $
           anchor, character classes and quoted blanks work.
test       t/007-regex-features.sh

assertion  XCU.lex.008
anchor     utilities/lex.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       CD
since      1992
says       Code in %{ %} and indented lines of the definitions is copied,
           indented code before the first rule runs on each entry to yylex,
           user subroutines are copied, and table size declarations are
           accepted.
test       t/008-user-code.sh

assertion  XCU.lex.009
anchor     utilities/lex.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/lex.html#STDOUT
class      conditional
when       CD
since      1992
says       -n is accepted and the program is still written; with -t and -v
           the statistics go to standard error so standard output is still a
           valid C program.
test       t/009-options-n-v.sh

assertion  XCU.lex.010
anchor     utilities/lex.html#EXIT STATUS
class      conditional
when       CD
since      1992
says       A file operand that cannot be read gives a non-zero exit status.
test       t/010-missing-file.sh
